WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:31.283 --> 00:00:32.534
Good afternoon.

2
00:00:39.124 --> 00:00:42.127
Sorry, I was waiting for you to ask if--
if I needed anything.

3
00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:45.338
So, this is my mom
and dad's favorite restaurant

4
00:00:45.422 --> 00:00:48.341
and Friday's
their 35th wedding anniversary, Jade.

5
00:00:48.425 --> 00:00:50.302
How do you know my name?

6
00:00:51.219 --> 00:00:54.431
Oh, I don't. That's what
the 35th wedding anniversary is:

7
00:00:54.514 --> 00:00:55.515
Jade.

8
00:00:55.599 --> 00:00:59.019
Oh, weird. What time, then?

9
00:00:59.102 --> 00:01:02.480
Oh, 7:30, three people and really wanna
make sure we get the window table.

10
00:01:06.902 --> 00:01:08.445
You've got all the divisions…

11
00:01:08.528 --> 00:01:09.905
I have to talk to Derrick.

12
00:01:09.988 --> 00:01:11.615
…former England international…

13
00:01:12.324 --> 00:01:13.575
Chris Kamara.

14
00:01:13.658 --> 00:01:15.702
It was an unbelievable performance.

15
00:01:15.785 --> 00:01:17.913
Do you mind just turning that up?
Thank you.

16
00:01:17.996 --> 00:01:20.123
I couldn't believe it!

17
00:01:20.206 --> 00:01:21.458
Looking into the championship now,

18
00:01:21.541 --> 00:01:23.835
Roy, your old mob in Richmond, struggling.

19
00:01:23.919 --> 00:01:26.421
There are a lot of theories
as to why that might be.

20
00:01:26.504 --> 00:01:29.466
One that's gaining traction
is a lack of leadership

21
00:01:29.549 --> 00:01:31.843
from your successor as captain,
Isaac McAdoo.

22
00:01:31.927 --> 00:01:35.388
Isaac's a good lad. He'll find his way.

23
00:01:35.472 --> 00:01:39.017
You know, under Ted Lasso, Richmond, well,

24
00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:42.354
they're like a woman behind the wheel:
completely lost!

25
00:01:42.437 --> 00:01:45.732
George! Didn't you lose your license
drink driving?

26
00:01:46.316 --> 00:01:48.902
That was an allergic reaction
to my medication.

27
00:01:48.985 --> 00:01:50.904
The same medication
that made you piss your pants?

28
00:01:56.243 --> 00:01:57.494
Nothing coming up…

29
00:01:57.577 --> 00:01:58.995
So, did-- Did the--

30
00:02:01.915 --> 00:02:03.250
Hey. Hi.

31
00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:05.210
Good news.

32
00:02:05.293 --> 00:02:07.796
We can set aside
the table in the corner for you.

33
00:02:08.462 --> 00:02:10.006
Wonderful. I just--

34
00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:13.134
I would really like the window table,
you know, just to impress my dad.

35
00:02:13.218 --> 00:02:16.680
I'm sorry. I can't guarantee a reservation
for the window table.

36
00:02:18.598 --> 00:02:20.642
I know Roy Kent, if that's--

37
00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:23.061
Is he your dad?

38
00:02:23.144 --> 00:02:24.229
No.

39
00:02:24.312 --> 00:02:27.482
Well, please let us know
if Mr. Kent ever wants the window table.

40
00:02:32.153 --> 00:02:33.280
Okay. Thank you.

41
00:03:29.336 --> 00:03:31.922
Jan Maas, that's shit defending.

42
00:03:32.005 --> 00:03:33.632
Yes, that goal was entirely my fault.

43
00:03:33.715 --> 00:03:36.676
I don't wanna hear it.
We need to get our shit together!

44
00:03:38.553 --> 00:03:40.931
Hey, hit pause for me, will you?
Hey, fellas.

45
00:03:41.514 --> 00:03:43.183
No, I gave you an indoor whistle.

46
00:03:43.266 --> 00:03:45.143
Listen, I don't care what our record is,

47
00:03:45.227 --> 00:03:48.063
but I hear the chatter, people saying
there's something wrong with us.

48
00:03:48.146 --> 00:03:49.731
Not the way I see it, okay?

49
00:03:49.814 --> 00:03:50.857
And here's why:

50
00:03:50.941 --> 00:03:52.609
I believe in communism.

51
00:03:55.028 --> 00:03:56.696
Rom-communism, that is.

52
00:03:58.114 --> 00:03:59.616
What is rom-communism?

53
00:03:59.699 --> 00:04:01.910
Well, Bumbercatch,
it is a worldview that reminds us

54
00:04:01.993 --> 00:04:05.914
that romantic comedies with folks
like Tom Hanks, Meg Ryan

55
00:04:05.997 --> 00:04:08.583
or Julia Roberts and Hugh Grant or--
Who am I missing, Coach?

56
00:04:09.751 --> 00:04:11.086
Drew Barrymore?

57
00:04:11.169 --> 00:04:13.713
-Matthew McConaughey, obviously.
-All right, all right. Yeah.

58
00:04:13.797 --> 00:04:16.091
-The three Kates.
-Yeah, Beckinsale, Hudson, Winslet.

59
00:04:17.007 --> 00:04:19.219
-You forgot Blanchett.
-Different spelling.

60
00:04:19.302 --> 00:04:21.721
I enjoy Renée Zellweger
and all the Bridget Jones movies.

61
00:04:22.347 --> 00:04:23.682
I mean, her accent is pitch perfect

62
00:04:23.765 --> 00:04:25.934
and her gift of physical comedy
is grossly underrated.

63
00:04:26.017 --> 00:04:27.978
-Word!
-Hell yeah!

64
00:04:28.061 --> 00:04:29.312
-Absolutely!
-I saw Judy…

65
00:04:29.396 --> 00:04:31.147
All right,
you've gotta give it up for Zellweger.

66
00:04:32.399 --> 00:04:34.859
Look, point is, fellas,
if all those attractive people

67
00:04:34.943 --> 00:04:37.320
with their amazing apartments
and interesting jobs,

68
00:04:37.404 --> 00:04:38.905
usually in some creative field,

69
00:04:38.989 --> 00:04:42.325
can go through some lighthearted struggles
and still end up happy,

70
00:04:42.409 --> 00:04:43.410
then so can we.

71
00:04:44.494 --> 00:04:45.579
Jennifer Lopez!

72
00:04:46.538 --> 00:04:48.790
That's a great call, Dani,
and not at all a beat too late.

73
00:04:49.916 --> 00:04:51.835
Gentlemen, believing in rom-communism

74
00:04:51.918 --> 00:04:54.588
is all about believing that everything's
gonna work out in the end.

75
00:04:54.671 --> 00:04:56.756
Now these next few months might be tricky,

76
00:04:57.465 --> 00:04:59.467
but that's just 'cause
we're going through our dark forest.

77
00:04:59.551 --> 00:05:02.804
Fairy tales do not start,
nor do they end in the dark forest.

78
00:05:02.888 --> 00:05:06.099
That son of a gun always shows up
smack-dab in the middle of a story.

79
00:05:06.182 --> 00:05:07.434
But it will all work out.

80
00:05:07.517 --> 00:05:09.060
Now, it may not work out

81
00:05:09.144 --> 00:05:12.355
how you think it will
or how you hope it does,

82
00:05:12.439 --> 00:05:16.860
but believe me, it will all work out.

83
00:05:17.485 --> 00:05:18.820
Exactly as it's supposed to.

84
00:05:20.947 --> 00:05:25.368
Our job is to have zero expectations
and just let go.

85
00:05:28.663 --> 00:05:29.664
Now, you heard him!

86
00:05:30.957 --> 00:05:32.876
We need to stop playing like shit!

87
00:05:32.959 --> 00:05:36.296
Yeah, not exactly what I said,
but I appreciate you, Isaac.

88
00:05:36.379 --> 00:05:38.965
Okay, let's watch the second half.
Come on, Coach.

89
00:05:44.137 --> 00:05:46.097
Hey, anyone know
what's going on with Isaac?

90
00:05:46.181 --> 00:05:47.641
I got no idea. No.

91
00:05:47.724 --> 00:05:49.643
Maybe it's piles.

92
00:05:49.726 --> 00:05:54.022
I've accepted "aubergine" and "snogging",
but "piles" I will not abide.

93
00:05:54.606 --> 00:05:57.317
Wait a second,
we play Sheffield Wednesday?

94
00:05:57.400 --> 00:06:00.028
-Saturday.
-Oh, we're playing Sheffield Saturday?

95
00:06:00.111 --> 00:06:01.696
Sheffield Wednesday, Saturday.

96
00:06:01.780 --> 00:06:03.531
We gotta play 'em twice in the same week?

97
00:06:05.533 --> 00:06:07.911
The club is called Sheffield Wednesday.
We play them on Saturday.

98
00:06:07.994 --> 00:06:10.872
They're called Sheffield Wednesday because
they used to only play on Wednesdays.

99
00:06:10.956 --> 00:06:13.124
But nowadays they play on
whatever day they feel like,

100
00:06:13.208 --> 00:06:15.085
including, but not limited to, Saturdays,

101
00:06:15.168 --> 00:06:17.295
which, again, is the day
we will be playing them.

102
00:06:17.379 --> 00:06:18.964
This Saturday? I can't. I got plans.

103
00:06:19.714 --> 00:06:21.007
-I'm leaving.
-Oh, come on.

104
00:06:21.550 --> 00:06:23.134
-Hey, Doc.
-Good afternoon.

105
00:06:23.802 --> 00:06:25.887
Coach Lasso, is Isaac okay?

106
00:06:25.971 --> 00:06:27.347
No, ma'am, he is not.

107
00:06:28.139 --> 00:06:30.225
He's a wigwam in a tepee right now.

108
00:06:30.725 --> 00:06:31.893
What does that mean?

109
00:06:31.977 --> 00:06:33.812
-He's too tense.
-Boom!

110
00:06:34.854 --> 00:06:36.648
He's wound tighter than my nan's hairnet.

111
00:06:37.774 --> 00:06:39.359
That only makes sense if you know my nan,

112
00:06:39.442 --> 00:06:42.487
but when she wears a hairnet, it looks
like puppies are trying to escape from it.

113
00:06:44.656 --> 00:06:45.740
I am not crazy.

114
00:06:46.908 --> 00:06:49.744
-Do you want me to talk to Isaac?
-No. That's okay. We got it.

115
00:06:49.828 --> 00:06:51.705
I know exactly what Isaac needs.
Thank you, though.

116
00:06:52.581 --> 00:06:53.582
Okay.

117
00:06:56.585 --> 00:06:58.628
-What does Isaac need?
-Oh, I have no idea.

118
00:06:59.379 --> 00:07:00.547
No, usually in this situation

119
00:07:00.630 --> 00:07:03.300
I'd have a player talk to the team captain
before I intervened.

120
00:07:03.383 --> 00:07:05.010
-But Isaac's our captain.
-Exactly.

121
00:07:05.093 --> 00:07:07.345
And I can't very well
ask Isaac to pull himself aside.

122
00:07:07.429 --> 00:07:10.015
'Cause that would be dangerously close
to messing with the, what's it?

123
00:07:10.098 --> 00:07:11.766
-The dark arts?
-No, no.

124
00:07:11.850 --> 00:07:13.059
Space-time continuum?

125
00:07:13.143 --> 00:07:14.436
That's it, yeah.

126
00:07:14.978 --> 00:07:17.230
-Oh.
-Fact is, Isaac is a big dog, you know?

127
00:07:17.314 --> 00:07:19.441
So he's only going to
respond to a big dog himself.

128
00:07:22.527 --> 00:07:23.528
I'll do it.

129
00:07:27.198 --> 00:07:28.283
Oh, you're being serious?

130
00:07:29.367 --> 00:07:30.452
You didn't laugh.

131
00:07:30.535 --> 00:07:32.037
-You knew he was being serious?
-Yeah, man.

132
00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:33.496
Shoot. Busted.

133
00:07:34.789 --> 00:07:38.084
I'm sorry about that, Nate.
But I do appreciate the offer, you know?

134
00:07:38.168 --> 00:07:39.836
I think we gotta get him a real big dog.

135
00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:41.922
Yeah, no, goo-- Me too.

136
00:07:42.005 --> 00:07:43.840
-Yeah. Yeah. Thanks.
-Yeah.

137
00:07:43.924 --> 00:07:46.301
Okay. Let's see here.

138
00:07:47.969 --> 00:07:49.471
I'm okay with "fanny".

139
00:07:51.723 --> 00:07:54.226
One, two, three…

140
00:07:58.563 --> 00:07:59.773
Did you just giggle?

141
00:08:00.607 --> 00:08:01.858
I don't know. Did I?

142
00:08:03.026 --> 00:08:04.027
Maybe.

143
00:08:04.569 --> 00:08:06.404
And now you're doubling down
as Shy Rebecca,

144
00:08:06.488 --> 00:08:07.864
who is a fictional character.

145
00:08:07.948 --> 00:08:09.950
She does not actually exist,
so something's up.

146
00:08:12.244 --> 00:08:13.245
Hey, boys!

147
00:08:13.328 --> 00:08:15.705
Come get your free
Nespresso coffee machines

148
00:08:15.789 --> 00:08:17.499
because I'm amazing at my job!

149
00:08:17.582 --> 00:08:20.877
People who are amazing at their job
don't have to point it out.

150
00:08:21.461 --> 00:08:25.131
Actually, that's not how it works anymore.
It's all about promoting your own brand.

151
00:08:26.550 --> 00:08:29.219
Please don't forget to post
when you make yourselves an Americano.

152
00:08:29.302 --> 00:08:30.887
I'll put something
on my Insta straightaway.

153
00:08:30.971 --> 00:08:32.013
Thanks, Colin. Oh, wait!

154
00:08:32.681 --> 00:08:35.433
Do you think you can make this one post
not about Welsh independence?

155
00:08:36.268 --> 00:08:37.269
Yeah.

156
00:08:38.477 --> 00:08:39.520
Thank you.

157
00:08:40.145 --> 00:08:43.525
So can I, like, give this back to you
and you give me cash?

158
00:08:43.608 --> 00:08:45.193
-Is that a thing, or…
-No.

159
00:08:45.277 --> 00:08:47.070
Oh, yeah. Ok-- Okay.

160
00:08:49.072 --> 00:08:50.532
All right, what the fuck?

161
00:08:50.615 --> 00:08:53.868
Sorry. It's just this mystery man
that I've been talking to on Bantr

162
00:08:53.952 --> 00:08:56.246
has just quoted Rilke.

163
00:08:56.871 --> 00:08:59.916
"Our deepest fears are like dragons
guarding our deepest treasures".

164
00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:02.043
Oh, that is so hot.

165
00:09:03.086 --> 00:09:06.715
Maybe you're writing letters
to a hung poet.

166
00:09:07.340 --> 00:09:08.967
Is that a joke from Sex and The City?

167
00:09:09.050 --> 00:09:10.594
No, but thank you.

168
00:09:10.677 --> 00:09:12.137
I love that you're so excited.

169
00:09:12.220 --> 00:09:16.057
That's so Bantr,
a place where minds can come to undress.

170
00:09:16.141 --> 00:09:17.726
That's really good. I'm gonna use that.

171
00:09:17.809 --> 00:09:18.852
I mean, don't get me wrong,

172
00:09:18.935 --> 00:09:22.647
I'm still chatting to these other guys
on the other dating app, Tumescent.

173
00:09:22.731 --> 00:09:24.316
Yeah, and what was that discourse like?

174
00:09:25.317 --> 00:09:27.444
Less revealing, but more revealing.

175
00:09:28.278 --> 00:09:29.529
Jesus, where's the rest of it?

176
00:09:31.072 --> 00:09:32.073
Christ.

177
00:09:32.157 --> 00:09:34.618
I mean, shouldn't romance
have a little mystery to it?

178
00:09:35.785 --> 00:09:37.120
Sure, it depends on what you want.

179
00:09:38.038 --> 00:09:41.082
See? It all comes back to branding,
even with love.

180
00:09:42.751 --> 00:09:43.752
Yeah.

181
00:09:46.963 --> 00:09:48.882
Oh, Dani! Enjoy your free coffee.

182
00:09:48.965 --> 00:09:52.010
Oh, I don't drink coffee.
My mother says I was born caffeinated.

183
00:09:52.093 --> 00:09:53.637
Is it okay if I give it to my neighbor?

184
00:09:53.720 --> 00:09:55.639
She also doesn't drink coffee
but her son does.

185
00:09:55.722 --> 00:09:57.724
And she's trying to encourage
more visits from him.

186
00:09:57.807 --> 00:09:58.975
Sure!

187
00:09:59.059 --> 00:10:00.769
-¡Excelente!
-Oh, yeah!

188
00:10:00.852 --> 00:10:02.896
-Oh, wow. Look at this.
-Sorry, Nate.

189
00:10:02.979 --> 00:10:04.648
They're actually just for the players.

190
00:10:04.731 --> 00:10:06.566
Oh, good.

191
00:10:06.650 --> 00:10:09.110
I hate free coffee anyway,
always tastes so…

192
00:10:11.947 --> 00:10:13.156
Yeah. Fine.

193
00:10:34.761 --> 00:10:35.762
Hello, Rebecca.

194
00:10:36.680 --> 00:10:37.681
Hello, Higgins.

195
00:10:38.348 --> 00:10:39.432
What can I help you with?

196
00:10:39.516 --> 00:10:40.976
Payroll.

197
00:10:42.310 --> 00:10:45.146
We have an inquiry from AFC Wrexham.

198
00:10:45.230 --> 00:10:47.274
Just got a call from their new owners,

199
00:10:47.357 --> 00:10:49.734
showbiz magnates Rob McElhenney
and Ryan Reynolds.

200
00:10:50.485 --> 00:10:53.530
I can't tell if them buying the club
is a joke or not,

201
00:10:53.613 --> 00:10:55.115
so I haven't replied to them yet.

202
00:10:55.198 --> 00:10:58.451
Right.
Did you just see what was on my screen?

203
00:10:59.077 --> 00:11:00.620
Oh, no, no, no, no.

204
00:11:00.704 --> 00:11:02.414
I have five boys.

205
00:11:02.497 --> 00:11:05.208
I never look over anyone's shoulders
to see what's on their screens.

206
00:11:07.127 --> 00:11:08.211
I used to.

207
00:11:09.296 --> 00:11:10.297
Oh, apologies!

208
00:11:10.380 --> 00:11:12.424
That's my wife.

209
00:11:12.507 --> 00:11:14.676
I'll ring her back later. Keeps it fresh.

210
00:11:15.844 --> 00:11:18.513
But I'll just text her real quick
to let her know that.

211
00:11:19.306 --> 00:11:23.018
So your ringtone for your wife is
"She's a Rainbow" by the Rolling Stones?

212
00:11:23.101 --> 00:11:25.395
-Yeah.
-That's awfully affectionate.

213
00:11:25.478 --> 00:11:27.439
Yeah, well, it's our song.

214
00:11:27.981 --> 00:11:29.691
It was playing the moment we met.

215
00:11:29.774 --> 00:11:33.528
And it's not an exaggeration.
She really is my rainbow.

216
00:11:34.988 --> 00:11:37.616
It is so odd to imagine you young.

217
00:11:37.699 --> 00:11:39.326
Yeah, I get that a lot.

218
00:11:39.409 --> 00:11:41.661
I was the only kid in primary school
with sciatica.

219
00:11:42.829 --> 00:11:45.081
I had a gelatinous L4 and five.

220
00:11:46.625 --> 00:11:48.376
Leslie, do you mind me asking,

221
00:11:48.460 --> 00:11:50.295
when you first met your wife,

222
00:11:50.378 --> 00:11:53.131
how did you put yourself across?

223
00:11:53.215 --> 00:11:55.675
You know, what was your brand?

224
00:11:55.759 --> 00:11:56.968
"Brand"?

225
00:11:57.594 --> 00:12:00.305
Well, you know, the night I met my wife,

226
00:12:00.388 --> 00:12:04.309
I was attempting to be a brooding punk
with hair spiked out to here.

227
00:12:04.392 --> 00:12:08.813
And then "She's a Rainbow" came on
and I started playing upright air bass

228
00:12:08.897 --> 00:12:12.234
but I had a pint in my hand and ended up
pouring beer all over my head.

229
00:12:13.360 --> 00:12:15.111
Everyone in the bar laughed,

230
00:12:15.195 --> 00:12:19.407
except one person who handed me
a damp, disgusting bar towel.

231
00:12:20.992 --> 00:12:23.203
And I've been married to her for 29 years.

232
00:12:25.205 --> 00:12:29.960
I suppose…
the best brand is just being yourself.

233
00:12:52.440 --> 00:12:54.150
It's fine.

234
00:13:08.623 --> 00:13:10.333
-Nate?
-Yeah?

235
00:13:10.417 --> 00:13:11.418
Do you need something?

236
00:13:11.501 --> 00:13:14.629
No, me? No, me? No, thank you. No, but--

237
00:13:19.593 --> 00:13:22.387
Actually, there is possibly one thing
you might be able to help with.

238
00:13:22.470 --> 00:13:23.555
Yeah, come sit down.

239
00:13:23.638 --> 00:13:24.890
Oh, thank you.

240
00:13:32.480 --> 00:13:33.565
Can you make me famous?

241
00:13:34.566 --> 00:13:36.818
No! Nate, you don't wanna be famous.

242
00:13:36.902 --> 00:13:37.944
I don't?

243
00:13:38.028 --> 00:13:40.780
No!
There'll be photographers all up your bum.

244
00:13:40.864 --> 00:13:42.032
Oh. Yuck.

245
00:13:42.115 --> 00:13:43.909
Yeah,
and tabloids going through your rubbish.

246
00:13:43.992 --> 00:13:44.951
I don't want that.

247
00:13:45.035 --> 00:13:47.329
-Groupies everywhere?
-That's not horrible.

