00:27:49.796 --> 00:27:52.299
by Phil Collins and Philip Bailey
to get dressed in the morning.

502
00:27:52.382 --> 00:27:53.842
-Makes sense.
-Yeah.

503
00:27:54.509 --> 00:27:58.680
It is a beautiful Saturday,
and we are playing Sheffield Wednesday.

504
00:27:58.763 --> 00:28:00.891
-Aka "The Owls."
-Hey, how 'bout that?

505
00:28:00.974 --> 00:28:02.601
Hey, you never finished your joke.

506
00:28:03.226 --> 00:28:04.227
What joke?

507
00:28:04.311 --> 00:28:05.770
What does a British owl say?

508
00:28:06.271 --> 00:28:07.314
Oh, right.

509
00:28:08.064 --> 00:28:10.025
Whom. Whom.

510
00:28:12.235 --> 00:28:13.320
Worth the wait.

511
00:28:30.253 --> 00:28:32.339
We had season tickets for Richmond.

512
00:28:32.422 --> 00:28:33.882
My family was well-off.

513
00:28:33.965 --> 00:28:36.176
I was a young punk
that snuck in every week.

514
00:28:36.259 --> 00:28:38.762
My father wanted us in
the best seats in the house.

515
00:28:38.845 --> 00:28:41.389
I sat there because she was there.

516
00:28:41.473 --> 00:28:43.808
My mother and my boyfriend were furious.

517
00:28:43.892 --> 00:28:46.061
They wanted to call security
to kick him out.

518
00:28:46.144 --> 00:28:47.979
But she insisted that I should stay.

519
00:28:48.521 --> 00:28:51.524
-And we fell in love.
-And we fell in love.

520
00:28:52.442 --> 00:28:55.153
Years later, a close friend of the family

521
00:28:55.237 --> 00:28:58.240
used the same story line
for the film Titanic.

522
00:28:58.323 --> 00:29:00.450
And we've been in litigation ever since.

523
00:29:01.076 --> 00:29:03.370
-Together.
-Together.

524
00:29:05.622 --> 00:29:07.999
-Come on, Richmond!
-Richmond!

525
00:29:24.099 --> 00:29:25.892
Just stop with the foreplay.

526
00:29:25.976 --> 00:29:28.270
Tell him you own Richmond
and that you're fucking fit.

527
00:29:42.534 --> 00:29:43.910
-Coach.
-Doctor.

528
00:29:43.994 --> 00:29:45.787
Floor. Ceiling.

529
00:29:45.870 --> 00:29:46.997
Trash can.

530
00:29:47.080 --> 00:29:48.164
Now you go.

531
00:29:48.873 --> 00:29:51.001
I was just checking in.
See how you're feeling.

532
00:29:51.084 --> 00:29:53.086
Oh, well, that's mighty nice of you.

533
00:29:53.169 --> 00:29:54.504
How am I feeling?

534
00:29:54.588 --> 00:29:55.589
I don't know, you know?

535
00:29:55.672 --> 00:29:58.758
I-- I'm just dealing with the terror
of knowing what this world is about,

536
00:29:58.842 --> 00:30:00.051
you know?

537
00:30:00.135 --> 00:30:02.596
Watching a few good friends
screaming to let them out.

538
00:30:03.805 --> 00:30:05.348
So, you're feeling under pressure?

539
00:30:05.432 --> 00:30:07.017
Ba ba ba be doo

540
00:30:08.059 --> 00:30:09.895
Well, my door is always open.

541
00:30:09.978 --> 00:30:11.021
Then why even have one?

542
00:30:11.104 --> 00:30:13.773
Heck, Coach Beard could take
that thing out for ya Jack Torrance style

543
00:30:13.857 --> 00:30:14.900
with eight good whacks.

544
00:30:14.983 --> 00:30:16.234
Five good whacks.

545
00:30:16.318 --> 00:30:18.528
Lumberjack World Championship qualifier,
baby!

546
00:30:19.821 --> 00:30:22.073
That man has had many lives, many masters.

547
00:30:22.157 --> 00:30:24.659
Oh, snap! Hottie alert. Look at this guy.

548
00:30:25.452 --> 00:30:26.995
Hot-cha-cha.

549
00:30:27.078 --> 00:30:28.413
Game day suit. I love it.

550
00:30:28.496 --> 00:30:29.789
Not too much?

551
00:30:29.873 --> 00:30:31.708
What? Too much class? No such thing.

552
00:30:35.128 --> 00:30:38.131
If you are out to describe the truth,
leave elegance to the tailor.

553
00:30:41.718 --> 00:30:45.388
Hey, I appreciate you checking in, Doc.
All right. Let's go, Greyhounds!

554
00:30:46.389 --> 00:30:47.599
And we're back.

555
00:30:47.682 --> 00:30:49.017
Let's round off the Premier League

556
00:30:49.100 --> 00:30:51.519
with Arsenal heading
on the road to Newcastle,

557
00:30:51.603 --> 00:30:54.731
where 17-year-old Matthew Kerr
will make his debut.

558
00:30:54.814 --> 00:30:58.235
They're calling him the Irish Ronaldo.
What can we expect today?

559
00:30:58.318 --> 00:31:01.321
Well, I think we can expect to see
a commanding performance from the lad.

560
00:31:01.404 --> 00:31:03.281
Roy, what do you think he'll do today?

561
00:31:03.365 --> 00:31:05.742
I don't know. He's 17.

562
00:31:05.825 --> 00:31:08.203
He'll probably have chips for dinner
and a wank before bed.

563
00:31:08.286 --> 00:31:10.455
Oh, apologies for the language.

564
00:31:10.538 --> 00:31:13.041
Roy, I was looking for some insight

565
00:31:13.625 --> 00:31:15.085
about how he'll play.

566
00:31:15.168 --> 00:31:16.461
I told you, I don't know.

567
00:31:17.837 --> 00:31:19.422
All we do is sit around here

568
00:31:19.506 --> 00:31:22.175
and guess what a bunch of little pricks
are gonna go and do out there,

569
00:31:22.259 --> 00:31:23.426
then we come back at halftime,

570
00:31:23.510 --> 00:31:26.763
and we complain 'cause they didn't do
exactly what we thought they'd do.

571
00:31:27.973 --> 00:31:29.266
We don't know.

572
00:31:30.934 --> 00:31:32.394
Of course we don't know.

573
00:31:34.354 --> 00:31:36.064
We're not in the locker rooms with them.

574
00:31:36.147 --> 00:31:37.482
We're not on the pitch with them.

575
00:31:37.566 --> 00:31:40.235
We can't look 'em in the eyes
and encourage them to be better

576
00:31:40.318 --> 00:31:42.487
than they ever thought
they were capable of being.

577
00:31:43.905 --> 00:31:44.906
We're just--

578
00:31:46.074 --> 00:31:48.618
We're just on the outside looking in.

579
00:31:50.370 --> 00:31:51.371
Judging them.

580
00:31:54.291 --> 00:31:55.542
Okay, Roy.

581
00:31:55.625 --> 00:31:59.921
Well, here's a look at your old team
warming up in an interesting new way.

582
00:32:00.005 --> 00:32:01.506
Hey!

583
00:32:13.935 --> 00:32:16.021
Look,
it's all pretty loosey-goosey, isn't it?

584
00:32:16.104 --> 00:32:17.188
Especially for a team

585
00:32:17.272 --> 00:32:19.524
that's at the business end
of the relegation zone.

586
00:32:19.608 --> 00:32:22.444
But it is good
to see McAdoo with a smile on his face.

587
00:32:22.527 --> 00:32:25.363
He's been a shadow of himself all season.

588
00:32:25.447 --> 00:32:27.866
I wonder what's gotten into him.

589
00:32:27.949 --> 00:32:29.868
Oh, dang.
Yeah, come on, now. Come on, man.

590
00:32:29.951 --> 00:32:32.370
Boom. Boom. Boom. Boom. Boom. Boom.

591
00:32:32.871 --> 00:32:33.872
Pow.

592
00:32:34.789 --> 00:32:36.666
There you go. All right. Gentleman.

593
00:32:41.046 --> 00:32:43.757
Bloody cold out there today.
Bet you don't miss that, Roy.

594
00:32:44.257 --> 00:32:45.300
What?

595
00:32:45.383 --> 00:32:47.636
Said,
I bet you don't miss the cold, hey, Roy?

596
00:32:49.221 --> 00:32:50.472
I miss all of it.

597
00:32:52.224 --> 00:32:53.225
'Scuse me.

598
00:32:54.100 --> 00:32:56.144
-What are you doing?
-I'm sorry, fellas.

599
00:32:56.728 --> 00:32:58.146
This isn't what I'm meant to do.

600
00:33:03.235 --> 00:33:04.236
Roy!

601
00:33:06.029 --> 00:33:09.032
Jeff, I have to go.

602
00:33:38.103 --> 00:33:40.272
Thank you. Cheers, Ben.

603
00:33:42.899 --> 00:33:44.734
-You're Roy Kent.
-No, I'm not.

604
00:33:45.777 --> 00:33:47.862
All right, I am. Take me to Nelson Road.

605
00:33:47.946 --> 00:33:49.155
No. Headed home.

606
00:33:49.239 --> 00:33:51.616
It's me anniversary, mate,
and I haven't bought a present.

607
00:33:55.745 --> 00:33:56.997
Fuck.

608
00:33:58.164 --> 00:34:00.375
Right, my wife loves cash.

609
00:34:00.458 --> 00:34:01.459
Cheers.

610
00:34:20.103 --> 00:34:22.521
Sorry, mate,
this is as far as I can get ya.

611
00:34:24.566 --> 00:34:27.485
I'll tell you the thing Nikki Sixx said
in the Mötley Crüe Behind the Music.

612
00:34:27.568 --> 00:34:29.613
-"You gotta date your wife."
-Thanks, Roy.

613
00:34:36.995 --> 00:34:38.246
Fuck!

614
00:34:39.331 --> 00:34:41.374
Fuck. Fuck.

615
00:34:45.711 --> 00:34:46.838
You see this new watch?

616
00:34:46.922 --> 00:34:49.257
You get me to Nelson Road
in ten minutes, it's yours.

617
00:34:49.340 --> 00:34:50.342
Get in.

618
00:35:08.568 --> 00:35:09.903
Cheers.

619
00:35:11.071 --> 00:35:12.364
No!

620
00:35:18.119 --> 00:35:19.746
-I've gotta get in there.
-Do you have a ticket?

621
00:35:19.829 --> 00:35:22.666
-I can't let anyone in without a ticket.
-I'm Roy Kent.

622
00:35:22.749 --> 00:35:24.042
-He does look like him.
-A little.

623
00:35:24.125 --> 00:35:25.252
Around the mouth.

624
00:35:25.335 --> 00:35:26.419
For fuck's sake.

625
00:35:29.965 --> 00:35:32.259
I believe you're holding a ticket
for Reba McEntire.

626
00:35:39.641 --> 00:35:41.685
Good to see you back, Reba.

627
00:35:43.436 --> 00:35:45.230
Dad. Dad.

628
00:35:48.400 --> 00:35:49.985
-Enjoy the game.
-Fuck you.

629
00:35:50.068 --> 00:35:51.069
It is you.

630
00:35:54.447 --> 00:35:56.157
Fuck. Fuck. Fuck.

631
00:36:36.406 --> 00:36:37.407
Look!

632
00:36:42.746 --> 00:36:45.206
Holy shit.

633
00:36:45.290 --> 00:36:48.835
He's here! He's there!
He's every fucking where!

634
00:36:48.919 --> 00:36:52.047
Roy Kent! Roy Kent!

635
00:36:52.130 --> 00:36:54.424
He's here! Here's there!
He's every fucking where!

636
00:36:54.507 --> 00:36:57.427
Roy Kent! Roy Kent!

637
00:37:19.783 --> 00:37:20.951
Hello, Coach.

638
00:37:22.285 --> 00:37:23.995
-Really glad you decided to--
-Shut up.

639
00:37:24.496 --> 00:37:25.705
Just shut up.

640
00:37:26.706 --> 00:37:28.416
You had me at "Coach."

